# Testing Checklist

## Do not test documentation

**Forbidden:** pytest (or any test) whose assertions are primarily "this markdown/README/doc contains string X" or "file Y links to Z". Documentation is validated by human review, not by grep tests. Never create `test_*_docs.py` or similar for new work; do not extend legacy doc contract tests.

## Python interpreter selection

- **Always prefer the project-local `.venv` when present.** Use `./.venv/bin/python -m <tool>` (e.g. `./.venv/bin/python -m pytest`, `./.venv/bin/python -m mypy .`, `./.venv/bin/python -m flake8`) instead of bare `pytest` / `mypy` / `flake8` or `python3 -m ...`.
- If `$VIRTUAL_ENV` is already exported, you may use the tools on `PATH` (they will resolve inside the active venv). Otherwise fall back to `./.venv/bin/python -m ...` explicitly.
- Only fall back to a system interpreter (`python3`) when neither `.venv` nor an active `VIRTUAL_ENV` exists. Never run the broken Windows shim (`/mnt/c/.../pyenv-win/shims/...`) from WSL.
- `./scripts/run_tests.sh` already auto-selects `.venv` — when you use it, you don't need to prefix anything.

## Quality gates

- Run `flake8` early or rely on `pytest -m lint` for the gate.
- Run `mypy .` and clear every reported issue.
- Use `pytest` for the full suite when confidence is needed.
- Scope to unit work with `pytest -m unit`; keep tests isolated and fast.
- Cover integrations via `pytest -m integration`; mock external services.
- Combine coverage with `pytest -m "unit or integration"` when reviewing.
- Execute `pytest -m e2e` only when end-to-end behavior must be proven.
- Align `pytest -m e2e` coverage with the flows listed in `docs/user_flows/index.md`; add scenarios when new UF files appear.
- Prefer `./scripts/run_tests.sh` for repeatable local runs.
- Launch `./scripts/run_e2e_tests.sh` when browser flows are required; the script automatically starts/stops the server.
- Configure server startup via `E2E_SERVER_COMMAND` env var or disable with `E2E_SERVER_DISABLED=true` for non-web projects.
- Share fixtures through `tests/conftest.py` to avoid duplication.

## Frontend test runner

- Run Vitest from the repo root via `npm --prefix frontend test -- --run <vitest-paths>` (paths are relative to `frontend/`, e.g. `src/lib/analysis/onnx/io/contract.test.ts`).
- Do not invoke `npm test` from `/home/kirill/survival-go` directly — there is no root `package.json`, only `frontend/package.json`.
